> parse match x { 0 => 1, 1 => 2, _ => 3 }
((x == 0) ? 1 : ((x == 1) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0 => 1, 0 => 2, _ => 3 }
((x == 0) ? 1 : ((x == 0) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0..5 => 1, 3..9 => 2, _ => 3 }
(((x >= 0) && (x <= 5)) ? 1 : (((x >= 3) && (x <= 9)) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0..5 => 1, 6..9 => 2, _ => 3 }
(((x >= 0) && (x <= 5)) ? 1 : (((x >= 6) && (x <= 9)) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0 => 1, 1 | 2 => 5, 3..9 => 7, _ => 9 }
((x == 0) ? 1 : (((x == 1) || (x == 2)) ? 5 : (((x >= 3) && (x <= 9)) ? 7 : 9)))
> parse match x { _ => 0, 1 => 2 }
((x == 1) ? 2 : 0)
> parse match x { 1 => 2 }
((x == 1) ? 2 : undefined)
  note: match has no default arm: other values are outside the domain
> parse switch x { 0: 1, 1: 2, default: 3 }
((x == 0) ? 1 : ((x == 1) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0 -> 1, 1 -> 2, _ -> 3 }
((x == 0) ? 1 : ((x == 1) ? 2 : 3))
> parse match x { 0 => 1, }
((x == 0) ? 1 : undefined)
  note: match has no default arm: other values are outside the domain
> parse match x { default => 1 }
1
> parse match x { -1 => 1, 0 => 0, 1 => 1, _ => 2 }
((x == -1) ? 1 : ((x == 0) ? 0 : ((x == 1) ? 1 : 2)))
> parse { x if x >= 0, -x otherwise }
((x >= 0) ? x : (-x))
> parse { 1 if x > 5, 2 if x > 0, 0 otherwise }
((x > 5) ? 1 : ((x > 0) ? 2 : 0))
> range match(x: u8) { 0..3 => x, 4..7 => 7-x, _ => 0 }
range of x >= 0 && x <= 3 ? x : x >= 4 && x <= 7 ? 7 - x : 0 -> u8:
  0..3   (4 distinct values)
  values: 0..3
  fits in u2
  over all 256 points of the domain
